  "description": "A derivative BIDS-iEEG dataset of per-seizure connectivity results computed from stereo-EEG recordings of patients with drug-resistant epilepsy evaluated at Vanderbilt University Medical Center. It provides windowed partial directed coherence and imaginary coherence across six frequency bands for peri-ictal and interictal periods, with seizure onset zone and propagation zone labels. The data accompany a study of how the collapse of interictal suppressive networks permits seizure spread.",
  "methods_description": "SEEG channels were re-referenced to a bipolar montage and bandpass filtered. Partial directed coherence was computed on 5 s windows from grey-matter channels in six frequency bands (delta through high gamma, up to 150 Hz), using a 1 s stride. For each seizure, 10 min before onset, the ictal period, and 10 min after offset were analyzed, along with an interictal clip.",
